-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 3 (Deferral of State Pension): regulations 4 to 12A.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- Parent-Act provisions taken as stated inputs, never guessed (they are not among the inputs):
--   * whether a person "falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act" (inherited a deferred pension and is offered the
--     choice between a lump sum and a pension), and the amount of a lump sum under section 8(4);
--   * the formula of section 17 of the 2014 Act: regulations 10, 11, 12 and 12A feed it. The encoding takes section 17 to
--     work in whole weeks of deferral, each earning an increment (a percentage of a weekly rate), so that the increase in
--     the weekly rate is the sum, over the periods, of whole weeks times increment. Regulation 11 and 12 speak of "a number
--     of whole weeks for the purposes of section 17(3)", and regulation 12A(2) of "the amount of an increment", which is
--     why the encoding reads section 17 that way; the multiplication itself is section 17's, not this instrument's (fork F11).
-- Duration conventions: a "period of three months starting on" a date runs from that date to the day before the
-- same day three months later (fork F7), and "28 days starting with" a date ends 27 days after it (fork F8).

§ `Part 3 -- Deferral of State Pension`

§§ `Regulation 4: when a choice may be made`

-- src:50 | (2) Where the Secretary of State has issued a notice which confirms that the person may make the choice, the period is three months starting on the date in that notice (or, where there is more than one notice which confirms that the person may make that choice, the date in the most recent such notice).
@ref Regulation 4(2) (src:50)
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period of three months starting on` `the first day` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of` 3 `months starting on` `the first day`

-- "(or, where there is more than one notice which confirms that the person may make that choice, the date in the most
-- recent such notice)". The list is the notices already issued when the choice is made.
@ref Regulation 4(2) (src:50)
GIVEN `the dates` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date in the most recent notice` `the dates` MEANS
    Date (maximum (map (GIVEN `a date` YIELD Day `a date`) `the dates`))

-- src:47 | (1) Where a person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act (choice of lump sum or survivor's pension under section 9 in certain cases), paragraphs (2) and (3) set out the period within which that person is to make any choice under section 8(2) of that Act to be paid—
-- src:48 | (a) a lump sum under section 8 of that Act; or
-- src:49 | (b) a state pension under section 9 of that Act (survivor's pension based on inheritance of deferred old state pension).
-- src:50 | (2) Where the Secretary of State has issued a notice which confirms that the person may make the choice, the period is three months starting on the date in that notice (or, where there is more than one notice which confirms that the person may make that choice, the date in the most recent such notice).
-- src:51 | (3) Where the person makes the choice before the Secretary of State has issued any such notice, the period—
-- src:52 | (a) starts on the later of the date—
-- src:53 | (i) the person claims a state pension; or
-- src:54 | (ii) the person's spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:55 | (b) ends on the date the person makes the choice.
@ref Regulation 4(1), 4(2), 4(3) (src:47-55)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for the period for a choice`
GIVETH A `Where a choice falls against its period`
`where the choice falls against its period` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   NOT (null (`the facts`'s `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice`))
    THEN IF   Day (`the facts`'s `the date the choice was made`) LESS THAN Day (`the date in the most recent notice` (`the facts`'s `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice`))
         THEN `before the period begins, which the text does not provide for`
         ELSE IF   Day (`the facts`'s `the date the choice was made`) AT MOST Day (`the last day of the period of three months starting on` (`the date in the most recent notice` (`the facts`'s `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice`)))
              THEN `within the period for making the choice`
              ELSE `after the period, so that it can only be a late choice`
    ELSE IF   Day (`the facts`'s `the date the choice was made`) AT LEAST Day (`the later of` (`the facts`'s `the date the person claimed a state pension`) (`the facts`'s `the date the spouse or civil partner died`))
         THEN `within the period for making the choice`
         ELSE `before the period begins, which the text does not provide for`

-- src:56 | (4) A person may make a late choice after the period set out in this regulation in circumstances where—
-- src:57 | (a) the Secretary of State considers it is reasonable in any particular case; and
-- src:58 | (b) any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act has been repaid to the Secretary of State—
-- src:59 | (i) in full; and
-- src:60 | (ii) in the currency in which that amount was originally paid.
@ref Regulation 4(4) (src:56-60)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for a late choice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a late choice may be made` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case`
    AND (    (NOT `the facts`'s `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum`)
          OR (    `the facts`'s `it has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full`
              AND `the facts`'s `it has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid`))

-- src:61 | (5) The amount of any lump sum to be paid to the person under section 8(4) is reduced to nil where the person makes a late choice under paragraph (4) to be paid a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 4(5) (src:61)
GIVEN `the lump sum` IS A NUMBER
      `the choice` IS A `Payment chosen`
      `it is a late choice under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lump sum to be paid after a choice, the amount being` `the lump sum` `and the choice being` `the choice` `and it being a late choice under paragraph (4)` `it is a late choice under paragraph (4)` MEANS
    IF   `it is a late choice under paragraph (4)` AND `the choice` EQUALS `a state pension`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the lump sum`

§§ `Regulation 5: how a choice may be made, and regulation 7(2) and (3): how a notice may be given`

-- The manner is the same relation in regulations 5 (a choice), 6(2)(d) (an application to alter a choice) and 7 (a notice
-- to suspend), and regulation 18(3) takes it over for Part 6. It is encoded once, here, and called from each.
-- src:66 | (2) The manner is—
-- src:67 | (a) in writing to an office which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such choice; or
-- src:68 | (b) by telephone to a telephone number which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such choice.
-- src:69 | (3) The person must use the manner set out in paragraph (2)(a) where the Secretary of State directs in any particular case that that manner must be used.
-- src:94 | (2) The manner in which the notice must be given is—
-- src:95 | (a) in writing to an office which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such notice; or
-- src:96 | (b) by telephone to a telephone number which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such notice.
-- src:97 | (3) But the person must use the manner set out in paragraph (2)(a) where the Secretary of State directs in any particular case that that manner must be used.
@ref Regulation 5(2), 5(3) (src:66-69); regulation 7(2), 7(3) (src:94-97)
GIVEN `how it was given` IS A `How something was given`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` `how it was given` MEANS
    IF   `how it was given`'s `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used`
    THEN     `how it was given`'s `the manner` EQUALS `in writing`
         AND `how it was given`'s `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it`
    ELSE     (    `how it was given`'s `the manner` EQUALS `in writing`
              OR  `how it was given`'s `the manner` EQUALS `by telephone`)
         AND `how it was given`'s `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it`

§§ `Regulation 6: changing a choice`

-- src:79 | (i) the period of three months starting on the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State which confirms the choice that has been made; or
@ref Regulation 6(2)(c)(i) (src:79)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application to alter a choice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application is made within the time allowed` `the application` MEANS
        (    Day (`the application`'s `the date the application is made`) AT LEAST Day (`the application`'s `the date in the notification confirming the choice that has been made`)
         AND Day (`the application`'s `the date the application is made`) AT MOST Day (`the last day of the period of three months starting on` (`the application`'s `the date in the notification confirming the choice that has been made`)))
    OR  `the application`'s `the application is made within a longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable`

-- src:84 | (e) where the application is to alter the choice so that it becomes a choice to be paid a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act has been repaid to the Secretary of State—
-- src:85 | (i) in full;
-- src:86 | (ii) within the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (c); and
-- src:87 | (iii) in the currency in which that amount was originally paid;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(e) (src:84-87)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application to alter a choice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the repayment condition for a change to a state pension is met` `the application` MEANS
        (NOT (`the application`'s `the choice the application would substitute` EQUALS `a state pension`))
    OR  (    (NOT `the application`'s `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum`)
         OR  (    `the application`'s `it has been repaid in full`
              AND `the application`'s `it was repaid within the period in paragraph (2)(c)`
              AND `the application`'s `it was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid`))

-- src:88 | (f) where the application is to alter the choice so that it becomes a choice to be paid a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act would be less than the amount which would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(f) (src:88)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application to alter a choice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amount condition for a change to a lump sum is met` `the application` MEANS
        (NOT (`the application`'s `the choice the application would substitute` EQUALS `a lump sum`))
    OR  `the application`'s `the amount paid by way of a state pension` LESS THAN `the application`'s `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum`

-- src:71 | (1) Any choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act to be paid—
-- src:72 | (a) a lump sum under section 8 of that Act; or
-- src:73 | (b) a state pension under section 9 of that Act,
-- src:74 | may be altered in the circumstances specified in paragraph (2).
-- src:75 | (2) The circumstances referred to in paragraph (1) are—
-- src:76 | (a) the person who made the choice has not subsequently died;
-- src:77 | (b) an application is made to alter the choice;
-- src:78 | (c) the application is made within—
-- src:79 | (i) the period of three months starting on the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State which confirms the choice that has been made; or
-- src:80 | (ii) such longer period as the Secretary of State considers reasonable in any particular case;
-- src:81 | (d) the application is made in the manner set out in—
-- src:82 | (i) regulation 5(2)(a), where the Secretary of State directs in any particular case that the manner in regulation 5(2)(a) must be used; or
-- src:83 | (ii) regulation 5(2)(a) or (b), in all other cases;
-- src:84 | (e) where the application is to alter the choice so that it becomes a choice to be paid a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act has been repaid to the Secretary of State—
-- src:85 | (i) in full;
-- src:86 | (ii) within the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (c); and
-- src:87 | (iii) in the currency in which that amount was originally paid;
-- src:88 | (f) where the application is to alter the choice so that it becomes a choice to be paid a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act would be less than the amount which would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act;
-- src:89 | (g) no previous alteration has been made under this regulation in respect of the same deferral mentioned in section 8(1)(c) of the 2014 Act; and
-- src:90 | (h) the choice has not been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987 (payments on death) .
@ref Regulation 6(1), 6(2) (src:71-90)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application to alter a choice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the choice may be altered` `the application` MEANS
        `the application`'s `the person who made the choice has not subsequently died`
    AND `the application`'s `an application is made to alter the choice`
    AND `the application is made within the time allowed` `the application`
    AND `it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`the application`'s `how the application is made`)
    AND `the repayment condition for a change to a state pension is met` `the application`
    AND `the amount condition for a change to a lump sum is met` `the application`
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `an alteration has already been made in respect of the same deferral`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987`)

-- Paragraph (3): where (2)(f) applies, what was paid as a state pension is treated as paid on account of the lump sum.
-- src:91 | (3) Where the circumstance in paragraph (2)(f) applies, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act in respect of the deferral mentioned in section 8(1)(c) of the 2014 Act for which the choice was originally made is to be treated as having been paid on account of the lump sum to be paid under section 8 of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 6(3) (src:91)
GIVEN `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount already paid by way of a state pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of the lump sum still to be paid, the lump sum being` `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum` `and the state pension already paid being` `the amount already paid by way of a state pension` MEANS
    `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum` MINUS `the amount already paid by way of a state pension`

§§ `Regulations 7 to 9: suspending entitlement`

-- src:93 | (1) A person who has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act may opt to suspend their entitlement if they give notice to the Secretary of State.
@ref Regulation 7(1) (src:93)
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `Notice suspending entitlement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`entitlement is suspended by a notice` `the notice` MEANS
        `the notice`'s `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act`
    AND `the notice`'s `the person has given notice to the Secretary of State`
    AND `it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`the notice`'s `how the notice was given`)

-- "not after 28 days starting with the date on which the option was exercised": the 28 days begin on that date, so the
-- last of them is 27 days later (fork F8).
-- src:102 | (b) not after 28 days starting with the date on which the option was exercised.
@ref Regulation 8(2)(b) (src:102)
GIVEN `the date on which the option was exercised` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last date the person may specify, the option being exercised on` `the date on which the option was exercised` MEANS
    Date (Day `the date on which the option was exercised` PLUS 27)

-- src:99 | (1) Where a person exercises their option to suspend their entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act, the suspension takes effect from the date set out in this regulation.
-- src:100 | (2) The date is any date which the person specifies that is—
-- src:101 | (a) not before the date on which the option was exercised; and
-- src:102 | (b) not after 28 days starting with the date on which the option was exercised.
-- src:103 | (3) Where the person does not specify a date in accordance with paragraph (2), the date is the date on which the option was exercised.
@ref Regulation 8(1), 8(2), 8(3) (src:99-103)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for the start of a suspension`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date from which the suspension takes effect` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the date the person specifies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the facts`'s `the date on which the option was exercised`
    WHEN JUST `a specified date` THEN
        IF       Day `a specified date` AT LEAST Day (`the facts`'s `the date on which the option was exercised`)
             AND Day `a specified date` AT MOST Day (`the last date the person may specify, the option being exercised on` (`the facts`'s `the date on which the option was exercised`))
        THEN `a specified date`
        ELSE `the facts`'s `the date on which the option was exercised`

-- src:105 | (1) Where a person has opted to suspend their entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act, the person may cancel the exercise of that option in relation to the whole of, or part of, a past period referred to in paragraph (3).
-- src:106 | (2) The person cancels the suspension by making a claim for their state pension whilst their state pension is suspended.
-- src:107 | (3) The past period mentioned in paragraph (1) is any period of up to 12 months before the date on which the person cancels the suspension.
@ref Regulation 9 (src:105-107)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for cancelling a suspension`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the suspension is cancelled for the past period` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the person opted to suspend entitlement`
    AND `the facts`'s `the person made a claim for a state pension whilst it was suspended`
    AND Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the past period`) AT MOST Day (`the facts`'s `the last day of the past period`)
    AND Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the past period`) AT LEAST Day (`add months` (`the facts`'s `the date on which the person cancels the suspension`) (0 MINUS 12))
    AND Day (`the facts`'s `the last day of the past period`) LESS THAN Day (`the facts`'s `the date on which the person cancels the suspension`)

§§ `Regulation 10: the percentage`

-- "one-ninth of 1%", exactly: a ninth of one hundredth.
-- src:109 | For the purposes of section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (effect of pensioner postponing or suspending state pension), the specified percentage is one-ninth of 1%.
@ref Regulation 10 (src:109)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the specified percentage for the increase in the weekly rate` MEANS (1 / 9) TIMES 1%

§§ `Regulation 11: days that are not counted`

-- src:112 | (2) The circumstances mentioned in paragraph (1) are where the day is—
-- src:113 | (a) a day on which the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred has received any of the following benefits—
-- src:114 | (i) state pension credit under section 1 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 (entitlement to state pension credit) ;
-- src:115 | (ii) income support under section 124 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (income support) ;
-- src:116 | (iii) an income-related employment and support allowance (which means an income-related allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (employment and support allowance) );
-- src:117 | (iv) an income-based jobseeker's allowance within the meaning in section 1(4) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (the jobseeker's allowance) ;
-- src:118 | (v) universal credit under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (universal credit) ;
-- src:119 | (vi) a carer's allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (carer's allowance) ;
-- src:120 | (via) the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023 (“carer support payment”);
-- src:121 | (vii) an unemployability supplement within the meaning in regulation 2(1) of the Social Security (Overlapping Benefits) Regulations 1979 (interpretation) ;
-- src:122 | (viii) severe disablement allowance under section 68 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (entitlement and rate of severe disablement allowance) ;
-- src:123 | (ix) a widow's pension under section 39 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (rate of widowed mother's allowance and widow's pension) ;
-- src:124 | (x) a widowed mother's allowance under section 37 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (widowed mother's allowance) ;
-- src:125 | (xi) incapacity benefit under section 30A of the Contributions and Benefits Act (incapacity benefit: entitlement) ;
-- src:126 | (b) a day on which a person—
-- src:127 | (i) has received an increase of any of the benefits mentioned in sub-paragraph (a) in respect of the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred; and
-- src:128 | (ii) is married to, in a civil partnership with or residing with the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred; or
-- src:129 | (c) a day on which the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, be paid that state pension because they were a prisoner (see section 19 of the 2014 Act (prisoners) and regulations 2 and 3).
@ref Regulation 11(2) (src:112-129)
GIVEN `the day` IS A `A day of the deferral period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` `the day` MEANS
        (NOT (`the day`'s `the benefit the person received on the day` EQUALS `none of those benefits`))
    OR  (    `the day`'s `an increase of one of those benefits was received in respect of the person on the day`
         AND (    `the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` (`the day`'s `the person who received the increase and the person whose entitlement is deferred`)
              OR  `the day`'s `they reside together`))
    OR  `a state pension is not to be paid for the day` (`the day`'s `the person's custody on the day`)

-- src:111 | (1) In the circumstances set out in paragraph (2), a day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks for the purposes of section 17(3) of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 11(1) (src:111)
GIVEN `the days` IS A LIST OF `A day of the deferral period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of the listed days that do not count` `the days` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN `a day` YIELD `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` `a day`) `the days`)

§§ `Regulation 12: part weeks`

-- src:132 | (2) The circumstances mentioned in paragraph (1) are where there is a part of a week in the total period during which the person's entitlement to a state pension was deferred, after any days have been discounted under regulation 11.
@ref Regulation 12(2) (src:132)
GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number rounded up to a whole number` `the number` MEANS
    0 MINUS FLOOR (0 MINUS `the number`)

-- src:131 | (1) In the circumstances set out in paragraph (2), a part of a week is to be treated as a whole week for the purposes of section 17(3) of the 2014 Act.
-- src:132 | (2) The circumstances mentioned in paragraph (1) are where there is a part of a week in the total period during which the person's entitlement to a state pension was deferred, after any days have been discounted under regulation 11.
@ref Regulation 12 (src:131-132)
GIVEN `the days in the period of deferral` IS A NUMBER
      `the days that do not count under regulation 11` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole weeks of deferral, there being` `the days in the period of deferral` `days, of which` `the days that do not count under regulation 11` `do not count` MEANS
    `the number rounded up to a whole number` ((`the days in the period of deferral` MINUS `the days that do not count under regulation 11`) / 7)

-- src:20 | “deferral period” means the period during which a person’s entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred;
@ref Regulation 1(4) deferral period (src:20)
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Deferral period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the deferral period` `the period` MEANS
    (Day (`the period`'s `last day`) MINUS Day (`the period`'s `first day`)) PLUS 1

§§ `Regulation 12A: a change in the rate that is not an up-rating`

-- src:135 | (2) Section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (amount of an increment for pensioner postponing or suspending state pension) is modified to provide that the amount of an increment for each modification period is equal to a percentage specified in regulations of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person, if their entitlement had not been deferred, would have been entitled immediately before the end of the modification period.
-- src:136 | (3) The first modification period begins at the start of the deferral period and ends immediately before the date of the first or only non-uprating change.
-- src:137 | (4) Further modification periods begin on the date of the most recent or only non-uprating change and end—
-- src:138 | (a) immediately before the end of the deferral period, where there is no subsequent non-uprating change; or
-- src:139 | (b) immediately before the date of the subsequent non-uprating change, where there is a subsequent non-uprating change.
@ref Regulation 12A(3), 12A(4) (src:136-139)
GIVEN `the start of the modification period` IS A DATE
      `the end of the deferral period` IS A DATE
      `the dates of the non-uprating changes still to come, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Modification period`
`the modification periods beginning on` `the start of the modification period` `and ending with the deferral period on` `the end of the deferral period` `given the changes` `the dates of the non-uprating changes still to come, earliest first` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dates of the non-uprating changes still to come, earliest first`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN LIST (`Modification period` WITH `first day` IS `the start of the modification period`, `last day` IS `the end of the deferral period`)
    WHEN `a change` FOLLOWED BY `later changes` THEN
        (`Modification period` WITH `first day` IS `the start of the modification period`, `last day` IS Date (Day `a change` MINUS 1))
        FOLLOWED BY `the modification periods beginning on` `a change` `and ending with the deferral period on` `the end of the deferral period` `given the changes` `later changes`

-- Paragraph (1): the regulation applies only where there is a change; with none, there is nothing to modify.
-- src:134 | (1) Subject to regulation 23, this regulation applies in cases where, at any time in the deferral period, the weekly rate of the person’s state pension, had the person’s entitlement not been deferred, would have changed otherwise than because of an up-rating increase (“a non-uprating change”).
@ref Regulation 12A(1) (src:134)
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Deferral period`
      `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Modification period`
`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the period` `given the non-uprating changes` `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first` MEANS
    IF   null `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `the modification periods beginning on` (`the period`'s `first day`) `and ending with the deferral period on` (`the period`'s `last day`) `given the changes` `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first`

-- Paragraph (2): "the amount of an increment for each modification period is equal to a percentage specified in regulations
-- of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person, if their entitlement had not been deferred, would have
-- been entitled immediately before the end of the modification period". The percentage is regulation 10's.
-- src:135 | (2) Section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (amount of an increment for pensioner postponing or suspending state pension) is modified to provide that the amount of an increment for each modification period is equal to a percentage specified in regulations of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person, if their entitlement had not been deferred, would have been entitled immediately before the end of the modification period.
@ref Regulation 12A(2) (src:135)
GIVEN `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the modification period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increment for each whole week of a modification period, the weekly rate being` `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the modification period` MEANS
    `the specified percentage for the increase in the weekly rate` TIMES `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the modification period`

-- Fork F11: the increase in the weekly rate from a period is its whole weeks times its increment (section 17 of the 2014 Act).
@ref Regulation 12A(2) (src:135)
GIVEN `the increment for each whole week` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole weeks in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increase in the weekly rate from a period, the increment being` `the increment for each whole week` `for` `the whole weeks in the period` `whole weeks` MEANS
    `the increment for each whole week` TIMES `the whole weeks in the period`
